x;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Food gets a second chance </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/3Ap3j7bVnJUD64LqAKPTrPfYXZQ=/0x0:1920x1080/1920x1080/2025/10/21/1761075188525.jpeg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of groceries coming out of the top of a heart shape.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>America tosses </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmVlZGluZ2FtZXJpY2Eub3JnL291ci13b3JrL3JlZHVjZS1mb29kLXdhc3RlP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9wIzp-OnRleHQ9RWFjaCUyMHllYXIlMkMlMjAxMDglMjBiaWxsaW9uJTIwcG91bmRzLGZvb2QlMjBpbiUyMEFtZXJpY2ElMjBpcyUyMHdhc3RlZC4/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBc389eb8c\" target=\"_blank\">94 billion pounds</a><strong> </strong>of its food each year.</p><ul><li><strong>But many local organizations</strong> and volunteers are redirecting that food and turning it into meals for people in need.</li></ul><p><strong>Why it matters: </strong>As nearly <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmVlZGluZ2FtZXJpY2Eub3JnL2h1bmdlci1pbi1hbWVyaWNhP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBb88aeb2e\" target=\"_blank\">50 million Americans</a> struggle with food insecurity — lack of consistent access to nutritious food — these local groups are tackling two problems at once: food waste and hunger.</p><p><strong>🍲 Zoom in: </strong>Cincinnati has a robust food rescue network. Local organizations recovered 17,629 tons of food in 2024 — the equivalent of 29 million meals, <em>Axios Cincinnati's Kristen Swilley <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL2NpbmNpbm5hdGkvMjAyNi8xMS8wOS9oYW1pbHRvbi1jb3VudHktZm9vZC13YXN0ZS1yZXNjdWU_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBcb4edec2\" target=\"_blank\">reports</a>.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Our Daily Bread,</strong> Cincinnati's largest soup kitchen, has relied entirely on  rescued and donated food from restaurants and businesses throughout its 41 years of operation. Demand has doubled since 2016.</li><li><strong>\"We literally could not</strong> do what we do without rescued food,\" executive director Georgine Getty says.</li></ul><p><strong>🧑‍🍳 In Portland, Ore., </strong>nonprofit Urban Gleaners says it rescues nearly 1.2 million pounds of food annually and distributes it to more than 8,500 families across the region each week, <em>Axios Portland's Meira Gebel <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL3BvcnRsYW5kLzIwMjYvMDkvMTAvNC1nbGVhbmVkLWFuZC1nb3VybWV0P3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe6bbc560\" target=\"_blank\">writes</a>.</em></p><ul><li><strong>The group even hosts</strong> events inviting local chefs to make gourmet dishes out of food that would have been discarded.</li></ul><p><strong>🎡 In Minnesota, </strong>a group called Loaves and Fishes rescued food that didn't get sold at the Minnesota State Fair, <em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY2JzbmV3cy5jb20vbWlubmVzb3RhL25ld3MvbWlubmVzb3RhLXN0YXRlLWZhaXItZm9vZC1sZWZ0b3ZlcnMvP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB91a96a11\" target=\"_blank\">CBS reports</a></em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY2JzbmV3cy5jb20vbWlubmVzb3RhL25ld3MvbWlubmVzb3RhLXN0YXRlLWZhaXItZm9vZC1sZWZ0b3ZlcnMvP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC91a96a11\" target=\"_blank\"></a>.</p><ul><li><strong>The food collected </strong>from fair vendors <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubG9hdmVzYW5kZmlzaGVzbW4ub3JnL3Jlc2N1aW5nLWZvb2QtYXQtdGhlLW1pbm5lc290YS1zdGF0ZS1mYWlyLz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd848a228\" target=\"_blank\">included</a> french fries, cheese curds and bags of milk<em>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>⚽ In Philadelphia, </strong>20,000 pounds of surplus food from the World Cup was  delivered to families in need. Many other host cities organized similar efforts.</p><ul><li><strong>The stadium donated </strong>nearly 14,000 pre-made meals, which included salads, wraps, cookies, chips and gluten-free options. Those meals had been made for players and staff from teams including France, Brazil, Croatia and Haiti, <em>Axios Philadelphia's Mike D'Onofrio </em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL3BoaWxhZGVscGhpYS8yMDI2LzA3LzA4L3dvcmxkLWN1cC1mb29kLWJhbmtzLWRvbmF0aW9ucy1waGlsbHk_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa020f9a0\" target=\"_blank\"><em>reports</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2xvY2FsP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB8f9f6027\" target=\"_blank\">Find your Axios Local city</a> for news about your community.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtMDczMWU4YzctODAwYy00Zjg2LTgwZTgtNWUxNjc0MGIwNjMzLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB5514063c\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.381009/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48411790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Food gets a second chance&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20ha